// PVS-Studio diagnostic configuration for CI and IDE (pvs-studio-dotnet -C / solution .pvsconfig).
// Exclude generated and build artifacts from analysis.
//V_EXCLUDE_PATH **/bin/**
//V_EXCLUDE_PATH **/obj/**
//V_EXCLUDE_PATH **/*.g.cs
//V_EXCLUDE_PATH **/*.AssemblyInfo.cs
//V_EXCLUDE_PATH **/AssemblyInfo.cs
// Keep analysis aligned with the production CI project set (tests/samples/benchmarks out of scope).
//V_EXCLUDE_PATH **/tests/**
//V_EXCLUDE_PATH **/samples/**
//V_EXCLUDE_PATH **/benchmarks/**
//
// Empty best-effort catch blocks (dispose/drain/cleanup) are intentional and comment-documented.
// V3163 = GA; V5606 = OWASP twin of the same pattern.
// Correct disable syntax is //-V::NNNN (see PVS .pvsconfig manual).
//-V::3163,5606
//
// Reports include remaining groups/levels. CI fails only on GA:1,2 (see .github/workflows/ci.yml).
